Here, a basic agent template is created using the google adk

SETUP:
Open the terminal
-> pip install google-adk yfinance
-> adk create app

To run the contents of the app use command,
-> adk run app

We can integrate it with the web interface by using,
-> adk web
Other commands can be viewed in:
adk --help

  api_server           Starts a FastAPI server for agents.
  conformance          Conformance testing tools for ADK.
  create               Creates a new app in the current folder with prepopulated agent template.
  deploy               Deploys agent to hosted environments.
  eval                 Evaluates an agent given the eval sets.
  eval_set             Manage Eval Sets.
  generate_agent_card  Generates agent cards for all detected agents.
  migrate              ADK migration commands.
  optimize             Optimizes the root agent instructions using the GEPA optimizer.
  run                  Runs an agent.
  telemetry            Manage telemetry settings.
  test                 Runs pytest on agent test JSON files under the specified folder.
  web                  Starts a FastAPI server with Web UI for agents.

  Eg: adk web
  A url is provided 

COURSE AND EMAIL TOOLS:
The agent searches courses.json beside agent.py by default. Set
COURSE_CATALOG_PATH to use another JSON file containing an array of course
objects with fields such as code, name, and description.

Email sending uses SMTP. Configure SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT (default 587),
SMTP_USERNAME, SMTP_PASSWORD, and optionally SMTP_FROM (defaults to the SMTP
username). Keep credentials in environment variables, not in source files.
The agent must show the complete email draft and wait for an explicit YES from
the user before sending it.

  
